# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 (a function of a block reads the block's names and its own parameters) and ch. 8 (a widget applied is transparent: its places are the block's next): the row shows $count + $shown = 0 and gives 1; after the click both are 1, the row shows 2 and gives 3, in the click's own tick. The run on the gen1 f24a (fix ce1b0a05) gives these bytes.
test t

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="add")
    1: Ui.Label(text="row 0")
    2: Ui.Label(text="more 1")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="row 2")
    2: Ui.Label(text="more 3")
